// `emit_classify.vl` — the emitter's type classifiers and their supporting state: the
// `expr*` / `let*` / `declared*` / `param*` / `fnRet*` / `global*` families that resolve
// what VL type and rep a binding or expression lowers as. These are mutually recursive, so
// they share one module; the narrowing, scope, shape, ref-list and literal-atom classifiers
// they consult live in the `emit_*` modules imported below, which never import this one.
// Reads the AST arena (`ast.vl`) and the shared emitter state (`emit_state.vl`); writes no bytes.

// The character grammars over a type-name string come from `compiler/tyname.vl` directly,
// not through the republications in `emit_base.vl` and `typecheck.vl`.
// `isTopLevelFuncTypeName` stays out of it because it also writes the module-level
// `funcArrowAt` bank; `nameIsShapeSpanEnds` and `mapValNameOf`, because their span differs.
